   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r1040-opus, head 4fd56fb) : REQUEST CHANGES**\n\nThe code is sound. The only change I'm asking for is in the PR body: the `### Ledger` section is wrong.\n\n1. **Medium: PR #1040 body, `### Ledger`.** The entry is a `changelog` row. `CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md` lists *legacy problems that SwiftHFR fixes or changes on purpose*, and `export-app-changelog.py` turns it into the app's \"Nouveautés\" screen. This PR fixes no legacy problem: it brings back legacy's look, and it does so without legacy's link. Users would read \"comme avant\" as a new feature. Meanwhile GAP-055 (`GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md:78`) still says SwiftHFR shows a `\"Message cité N fois\" trailer (#819)`, which this PR makes out of date (L08/L09). **Fix:** replace the changelog row with a `gap-edit` on GAP-055, for example `SwiftHFR final: … count bubble at the right of the footer (#1039), not a link yet (quote_only=1 not captured, #126)`. If you keep a changelog row anyway, its kind is `UX`, not `T`.\n2. **Low: `TopicHTMLBuilderTests.swift:97` `aMessageNeverQuotedHasNoBubble`.** This test also passes without the change, because the old code never wrote `quoted-bubble` (L01). It works as a regression guard, but it proves nothing about this change. Say so in the PR's Tests section, or make it also check that no `<footer class=\"trailer\">` is written.\n3. **Detail: `reader.css:133-137`.** When the footer holds only the bubble, it sits right against the content: `.trailer p` has `margin-top: 0.25em`, the bubble has none. **Fix:** give `.quoted-bubble` `margin-top: 0.25em`.\n4. **Detail: `TopicHTMLBuilder.swift:228`.** `role=\"img\"` on a text span works: VoiceOver reads the label. A visually hidden text span would avoid announcing it as an \"image\". Optional.\n\nLeaving out the tap is justified. #1039 itself says to stop and open a capture issue if neither the legacy code nor a capture shows what the `quote_only=1` link returns. HFR-PROTOCOL §7 E2 and B11 say it is not captured, #126 is open, and the PR uses `Refs #1039`.\n\n**Verified:**\n- Read the diff, issue #1039 and the PR body.\n- Legacy @ 87fe0d1c: `LinkItem.m:237-238`, `ParseMessagesOperation.m:257`, and `style-liste.css:419-431`, which matches the citation.\n- Contrast: the bubble swaps the `--secondary` / `--background` pair, so its ratio equals the existing text one in every theme.\n- No JS reads `.trailer`.\n- `swiftlint lint --strict` passes on both Swift files, and no line is over 140 characters.\n- `ledger.py check-body` on the body: 1 block ok.\n- `trailersAndAvatar` cannot pass on the old code: the span it expects was not there.\n- Not run: the app tests. The app does not build on Linux, so CI compile-check decides.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
