   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r1040-opus, head e91c0ce) : APPROVE** — head e91c0ce\n\nRound 1 findings:\n1. **Ledger: fixed.** The PR body now has a `gap-edit` on GAP-055 instead of the `changelog` row. The id matches the row on line 78 of `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md`. The edited column, `SwiftHFR final`, is in the header on line 71. The new text keeps the existing border, padding and tint wording and only rewrites the \"Message cité\" part. `ledger.py check-body` on the posted body says: `1 block(s) ok`.\n2. **Guard test: fixed.** `aMessageNeverQuotedHasNoBubble` now also checks that no empty `<footer class=\"trailer\">` is written when the count is nil. The PR body says plainly that this test is a regression guard and passes without the change. `trailersAndAvatar` and `theBubbleIsNotALink` fail on the old code, as the body says.\n3. **Bubble top margin: fixed.** `reader.css:135` is now `margin: 0.25em 0 0 auto`, the same top margin as `.trailer p` on line 130.\n\nNew checks, no finding:\n- The new `.trailer { display: flex }` does not move the footer's left edge. `VisibilityWebTests.swift:275` only measures that left edge. The trailer's only other line is the edit note, so the flex row cannot pull lines out of order.\n- The bubble's HTML holds only an `Int`, so nothing needs escaping. It is not a link, which is right while `quote_only=1` is not captured (#126). The body says `Refs #1039` and that the tap is still to do.\n\nDetail (optional): the GAP-055 edit drops the old \"(#819)\" pointer from `SwiftHFR final`. You can put it back next to #1039.\n\n**Checked:** the full diff against `origin/dev-swift` and the round 2 change (4fd56fb..e91c0ce); `ledger.py check-body --file` on the PR body read through REST (head e91c0ce matches); the GAP table header and the GAP-055 row; the `gap-edit` format in `tooling/docs/README.md`; every use of `.trailer`, `quoted-bubble` and `quotedByCount` in `App/`; `swiftlint lint --strict` on the two changed Swift files (0 violations).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
